from lesson_writer import author,CPP
author('src/org/minima/system/brains/TxPoWMiner.md','Searches for a header hash below the transaction target, tracks coins reserved by mining and coordinates asynchronous mining messages.',[
 'Before queued or synchronous work, add unique input coin IDs from both main and burn transactions to a reservation list. This is a set-like list, not a per-job reference count: overlapping jobs can share one entry.',
 'Set the body hash, then use a deliberately large decimal nonce so its serialized field has room. Serialize the header once; each iteration copies the next BigInteger byte sequence beginning at byte offset four and hashes the full modified header with SHA3.',
 'Success requires hash < target, strictly. Decode the patched header to recover its resulting MiniNumber nonce, then set that nonce on the TxPoW and recalculate ID/size. The byte counter itself is not directly assigned as the final decimal nonce.',
 'Async processing posts a starting MAIN_MINING message before hashing. If the worker stops, the loop exits with final nonce zero but still performs the normal end/mined posts and reservation removal.',
 'The source adds automine to the starting message again when constructing the ending message. Consequently the ending message lacks that field. Retained-message identity matters to a faithful port.',
 'After async completion, automine schedules a pulse after the configured timer and a block-miner broadcast halfway through that delay. Pulse with no tip schedules a 30-second retry; TXBLOCK_NODE suppresses those generation branches.',
 'Synchronous mining ignores worker-running state and checks elapsed time only after 10,001 failed hashes. Timeout uses strict greater-than and returns immediately, retaining reservations and the initial large nonce. Other exceptions before cleanup can also retain reservations.',
 'Benchmark methods execute getAsInt(hashCount) iterations but use the original MiniNumber count as the speed numerator. Nonpositive measured elapsed time is replaced with one millisecond; a fractional or wrapped count therefore deserves a boundary test.'
], 'C++ reuses MessageProcessor/TimerMessage, real SHA3, BigInt Java byte encoding and TxHeader decoding. A service object binds Main, timers, generator, network, logs and clock. Shared messages retain TxPoW identity; a native mutex protects reservation access, while the pinned Java list has no equivalent per-method lock.',
 lambda l:'The '+l(CPP/'support/TxPoWMinerOracle.java','Java miner oracle')+', '+l(CPP/'support/txpow_miner.cpp','native harness')+' and '+l(CPP/'tools/txpow_miner_differential.py','driver')+' execute real mining loops with easy targets and impossible-target timeouts. They compare final wire/IDs, queued/retained messages, duplicate reservations, post failures, mutation before processing, stopped loops and timers. The inspected '+l(CPP/'build/txpow-miner-results.json','report')+' has 357 matching programs and 1,352 operations. Separately, '+l(CPP/'support/txpow_miner_worker.cpp','worker test source')+' asserts sixteen real queued results, ownership through cancellation, exception recovery, a strict timeout boundary, benchmark arithmetic and routing callbacks. Reading that test source is not a fresh run; the differential report does not include its assertions.',
 'Two jobs reserve the same coin. When the first finishes, why can the second still be active while checkForMiningCoin returns false? How would you preserve this source behavior without accidentally claiming it is a reference-counted reservation system?',
 'Full Main/network startup is incomplete. Java NPE expression text is normalized, arbitrary nonce-buffer exhaustion and concurrent Java races are not exhaustively matched, and the worker test supplies controlled routing receivers. Partial counterpart; parity not_verified.')
